  aidnexus: "No Redis/etcd lock service is used — the lease lives in the application database. Phase VI added scheduled_jobs.fence (migration v5) and made completion writes fenced. Before this, a stale holder could clear the new holder's lock and record a phantom run (regression test fails without the fence). Where a uniqueness constraint suffices (delivery receipts), no lock is used at all.",
  source: ["backend/app/scheduler.py::claim_job, finish_job_in", "backend/app/models_db.py::ScheduledJobRow.fence", "backend/app/migrations/versions/v5.py"],
  code: "update(ScheduledJobRow).where(job_name == name, fence == fence_token).values(...)\n# rowcount == 0  ->  stale_holder_rejected",
